  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Private Sector Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Regional Private Sector Development Programme works to embed private sector voice and leadership at the heart of Africa&apos;s trade agenda, recognising that sustainable and inclusive trade growth requires businesses, not just governments and institutions, to actively shape the policy environment, drive standards compliance, and unlock export opportunities across the continent. The Programme operates through a structured Private Sector Engagement Framework that provides a systematic approach to deepening collaboration between TMA, business associations, and enterprises at national and regional levels, with a particular focus on two complementary roles: enabling the private sector to identify, report, and advocate for the removal of non-tariff barriers and trade policy constraints in support of the Trade and Investment Environment Portfolio; and building enterprise capacity to meet international standards, access certification, and compete in regional and global value chains in support of the Quality and Value of Traded Goods Portfolio. Cutting across both, the Programme champions inclusive economic participation by implementing TMA&apos;s Gender and Inclusion Strategy to ensure that women-led enterprises, youth entrepreneurs, and underserved businesses are not only beneficiaries of trade reform but active participants in shaping it, in alignment with AfCFTA&apos;s continental market vision.</narrative>
  </description>
